  "cooked": "<p>In our <a href=\"https://www.dsn.kastel.kit.edu/bitcoin/#addresses\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">monitoring</a>, we see that the number of unique addresses being propagated in the network has risen noticeably during the last days:</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/original/1X/fe9ee15f6b983a1bf66e0a2c231c446f919b3adc.png\" data-download-href=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/fe9ee15f6b983a1bf66e0a2c231c446f919b3adc\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/fe9ee15f6b983a1bf66e0a2c231c446f919b3adc_2_690x376.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"AktFYLX5LirVnGLjduRM9EuxuGw\" width=\"690\" height=\"376\" srcset=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/fe9ee15f6b983a1bf66e0a2c231c446f919b3adc_2_690x376.png, https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/fe9ee15f6b983a1bf66e0a2c231c446f919b3adc_2_1035x564.png 1.5x, https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/original/1X/fe9ee15f6b983a1bf66e0a2c231c446f919b3adc.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"FAFAFA\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1110\u00d7605 37.4 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>This effect is probably caused by the peers that are described above in this topic.</p>\n<p>The observation indicates that the newly propagated addresses are unreachable and have not previously been announced in the network. Without having looked further into the set of distributed addresses I suppose that they might have been randomly generated.</p>",
